  "_notes": [
    "APPROXIMATE calendars - TO BE CONFIRMED against real Dukascopy data before production use. Expected-minute mismatches show up as INCOMPLETE/ERROR in the intake log.",
    "FX: America/New_York wall clock, open Sunday 17:00 to Friday 17:00 (covers the 22:00/21:00 UTC weekly boundary across DST). Intervals end at 24:00 or are split at local midnight.",
    "XAUUSD, US30, US500, USTEC: assumed daily maintenance break 17:00-18:00 New York time plus the weekly closure. Holidays are not modelled; add them under overrides.",
    "DE40: assumed Europe/Berlin Mon-Fri 01:00-22:00. Unverified guess.",
    "BTCUSD: 24/7, all seven days open.",
    "Inbox mode: drop paired '<SYMBOL>_1 Min_Bid_<from>_<to>*.csv' + '_Ask_' JForex exports into inbox_directory. source_directory is the read-only original history; only days after its last row are ingested.",
    "Paths are relative to this config file. first_day is a UTC date; days before the end of the original history are skipped regardless.",
    "providers: geordende terugvalketen uit 'datafeed', 'datafeed_ticks', 'jforex', 'inbox' (of enkelvoudig 'provider'). Zonder beide sleutels: inbox bij inbox_directory, jforex bij jforex_command of export_directory, anders datafeed."
